1
00:00:00,090 --> 00:00:05,200
[This series contains scenes of violence,
self-harm, and potential triggers. Viewer discretion is advised.]

2
00:00:03,790 --> 00:00:05,920
It's been a while, Herod.

3
00:00:07,050 --> 00:00:07,840
You are...

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,560
It's me, Jinyoung.

5
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:11,900
You don't remember?

6
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:13,460
That's quite sad.

7
00:00:14,340 --> 00:00:16,740
If I say this,
will you remember something?

8
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:18,860
That day in the school gym,

9
00:00:18,860 --> 00:00:21,420
before Adolph died, we were together.

10
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:23,340
The video taken back then—

11
00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:26,700
I was going to sell it to your CEO.

12
00:00:26,990 --> 00:00:29,300
But we were classmates after all.

13
00:00:29,990 --> 00:00:33,560
I thought I should
at least give my classmate a choice.

14
00:00:34,740 --> 00:00:36,590
I see you're quite popular lately.

15
00:00:36,590 --> 00:00:38,790
You must have made a lot of money, right?

16
00:00:41,150 --> 00:00:47,930
[Some scenes were created with AI.]

17
00:00:50,040 --> 00:00:53,780
[Adapted from the webtoon
"The Sound of Sugar Cubes" by Kim Tak]

18
00:00:53,810 --> 00:00:56,590
[Screenwriter: So-on (JD)]

19
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:59,550
[Director: Yoon Jinyoung]

20
00:01:16,110 --> 00:01:17,410
[Yoo Dohyun]

21
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:19,160
[Cho Chanhyeon]

22
00:01:19,289 --> 00:01:20,890
[Ko Gyeol]

23
00:01:22,520 --> 00:01:25,830
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

24
00:01:33,370 --> 00:01:35,820
With this, Hanyul can live.

25
00:01:36,190 --> 00:01:38,340
Without this, you can live, right?

26
00:01:44,690 --> 00:01:45,850
Take it.

27
00:01:54,940 --> 00:01:57,240
This is your only chance.

28
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:15,900
Take your hand off.

29
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:18,030
-No need.
-Seriously.

30
00:02:19,070 --> 00:02:20,130
Hey.

31
00:02:20,490 --> 00:02:21,250
Sorry.

32
00:02:21,390 --> 00:02:22,940
Next up is Herod's
emergency press conference.

33
00:02:22,940 --> 00:02:23,740
Hey, Herod...

34
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:25,030
What is he doing?

35
00:02:26,890 --> 00:02:40,000
[Herod holds an emergency press conference
to announce his official stance]

36
00:02:42,530 --> 00:02:46,380
Regarding the recent news
about Yul assaulting a classmate—

37
00:02:46,890 --> 00:02:49,030
I'm sure everyone's heard of it.

38
00:02:50,570 --> 00:02:52,070
Yul and I,

39
00:02:52,190 --> 00:02:54,130
along with the victim of the assault,

40
00:02:54,130 --> 00:02:56,329
were all classmates at the same school.

41
00:02:57,140 --> 00:02:59,050
We were very close friends, too.

42
00:03:01,510 --> 00:03:03,570
This is from the original video taken

43
00:03:03,830 --> 00:03:07,190
the day the assault occurred.

44
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:28,890
This loser.

45
00:03:29,410 --> 00:03:30,390
Where's Hanyul?

46
00:03:32,790 --> 00:03:35,030
I told him to stay with Adolph.

47
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:43,160
I bought snacks.

48
00:03:44,340 --> 00:03:45,400
What are you doing?

49
00:03:51,590 --> 00:03:54,530
This person... is me, right?

50
00:04:03,530 --> 00:04:04,700
Get up.

51
00:04:04,870 --> 00:04:06,360
Stop playing dead.

52
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:10,740
Hey, is he really dead?

53
00:04:10,860 --> 00:04:11,830
Whatever.

54
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:13,480
He's just an orphan anyway.

55
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:15,200
No one will notice if he's gone.

56
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:16,529
Didn't they say he and Lee Hanyul
were super close?

57
00:04:16,529 --> 00:04:18,459
Idiot, Lee Hanyul is an orphan too.

58
00:04:18,529 --> 00:04:19,970
But he's also close with Herod.

59
00:04:19,970 --> 00:04:21,690
Herod likes Lee Hanyul.

60
00:04:21,839 --> 00:04:24,720
But Lee Hanyul sticks
with this guy all day long.

61
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:27,370
He'd definitely be happy if this guy died.

62
00:04:27,900 --> 00:04:29,480
Oh, you're here.

63
00:04:30,030 --> 00:04:32,290
Look at his face. It's hilarious, right?

64
00:04:32,860 --> 00:04:38,390
Composing music, yeah right. When I saw him
playing the piano in the piano room I already thought...

65
00:04:53,390 --> 00:04:56,300
The person present that day
wasn't Yul, but me.

66
00:04:58,210 --> 00:05:01,230
Although I didn't participate
in the violence personally,

67
00:05:01,230 --> 00:05:03,640
I was indeed at the scene.

68
00:05:04,190 --> 00:05:06,080
In that moment, I hesitated.

69
00:05:06,990 --> 00:05:11,040
I turned a blind eye...
to my friend's suffering.

70
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:13,240
I am very sorry.

71
00:05:23,830 --> 00:05:27,690
Also, the song "Sound of Dawn"
that I released is not my original work.

72
00:05:28,440 --> 00:05:30,290
I stole my friend's song

73
00:05:30,420 --> 00:05:32,409
and released it under my own name.

74
00:05:33,100 --> 00:05:35,740
You might ruin your career and reputation.

75
00:05:35,850 --> 00:05:39,520
Why did you suddenly choose
to confess this right now?

76
00:05:39,860 --> 00:05:41,650
Are you trying to strike first

77
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:43,780
because you want to hide something else?

78
00:05:43,780 --> 00:05:46,380
Then who is the real creator
of "Sound of Dawn"?

79
00:05:46,430 --> 00:05:49,060
Is it this missing friend?

80
00:05:49,540 --> 00:05:51,150
Answer us.

81
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:54,430
Did you hold a press conference
just to talk to yourself?

82
00:05:56,420 --> 00:06:00,140
I stand here today to take responsibility
for everything.

83
00:06:01,750 --> 00:06:03,690
From today on,

84
00:06:04,270 --> 00:06:07,290
I will stop all entertainment activities

85
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:10,080
and leave the entertainment industry.

86
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:13,490
I will carry my apologies
to the victims for the rest of my life.

87
00:06:13,490 --> 00:06:16,390
I sincerely apologize to the victims

88
00:06:16,550 --> 00:06:19,920
and to Yul.

89
00:06:20,250 --> 00:06:22,950
Saying you'll take responsibility
is just an excuse.

90
00:06:22,950 --> 00:06:25,630
You just want to strike first
and run away, right?

91
00:06:25,630 --> 00:06:28,690
Do you mean you are willing
to accept legal punishment?

92
00:06:28,740 --> 00:06:31,830
Did your agency, Dawn Entertainment,
know and condone this?

93
00:06:31,830 --> 00:06:34,250
Is this an organized cover-up
at the company level?

94
00:06:34,250 --> 00:06:36,909
How exactly do you plan
to take responsibility?

95
00:06:37,180 --> 00:06:39,320
[Singer Herod admits
to school violence and song plagiarism]

96
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:40,370
Singer Herod
held an emergency press conference today,

97
00:06:40,409 --> 00:06:44,210
publicly admitting to standing by
while a classmate was assaulted,

98
00:06:44,230 --> 00:06:48,480
and to plagiarizing
the hit song "Sound of Dawn."

99
00:06:48,770 --> 00:06:50,700
He publicly admitted his mistakes

100
00:06:50,710 --> 00:06:53,500
and firmly stated he will
leave the entertainment industry.

101
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:55,550
But the subsequent impact
of this press conference

102
00:06:55,550 --> 00:06:58,620
will likely far exceed expectations.

103
00:06:58,850 --> 00:07:03,390
Especially since the police have officially launched
an investigation into Herod's agency for suspected organized collusion

104
00:07:03,390 --> 00:07:06,160
and deliberate concealment.

105
00:07:06,170 --> 00:07:07,180
Hanyul.

106
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:10,470
This company appears to be
a large entertainment agency on the surface,

107
00:07:10,470 --> 00:07:16,230
but is actually suspected to be a major money laundering channel
for a corporate syndicate.

108
00:07:10,810 --> 00:07:25,980
[Breaking News: Illegal loan organization using young children as collateral
is affiliated with an entertainment company suspected of laundering tens of billions]

109
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:21,420
While investigating the music distribution process
and the entire flow of funds,

110
00:07:21,590 --> 00:07:25,880
the police plan to focus on the origins
of the syndicate behind the agency.

111
00:07:32,850 --> 00:07:33,850
Where is Herod?

112
00:07:34,370 --> 00:07:36,030
He's not answering his phone.

113
00:07:40,860 --> 00:07:42,270
Did you do this?

114
00:07:43,159 --> 00:07:45,390
When you begged me for a week,

115
00:07:45,510 --> 00:07:48,650
was it actually to buy time
for this kind of trick behind my back?

116
00:07:48,650 --> 00:07:50,220
No, boss.

117
00:07:53,159 --> 00:07:55,100
Just to save that kid,

118
00:07:56,820 --> 00:07:58,820
you're going to betray the company?

119
00:07:59,220 --> 00:08:01,040
You're just a dog,

120
00:08:01,170 --> 00:08:02,970
and you dare to bite your master?

121
00:08:09,660 --> 00:08:11,370
It's not like that.

122
00:08:15,090 --> 00:08:16,470
Then were you...

123
00:08:16,630 --> 00:08:19,600
so blinded by that kid

124
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:23,730
that you couldn't even control
the mouth of a singer under the company?

125
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:28,820
This is dereliction of duty
and negligence, Lee Won!

126
00:08:40,169 --> 00:08:41,309
Kidneys,

127
00:08:41,580 --> 00:08:43,159
liver,

128
00:08:43,679 --> 00:08:45,110
corneas,

129
00:08:50,050 --> 00:08:52,520
and hair. Even if I sell all of these,

130
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:55,120
I'm still the one losing out.

131
00:08:56,940 --> 00:08:58,300
No.

132
00:08:58,630 --> 00:08:59,960
Chairman.

133
00:09:00,710 --> 00:09:03,410
You cannot touch him.

134
00:09:04,870 --> 00:09:06,040
All right then.

135
00:09:09,830 --> 00:09:12,660
Then... you die.

136
00:09:32,900 --> 00:09:35,140
What about you guys? Want some too?

137
00:09:37,730 --> 00:09:39,270
Why did you call him over?

138
00:09:39,990 --> 00:09:41,020
What's wrong?

139
00:09:41,150 --> 00:09:43,280
I called my friend to my hospital room,

140
00:09:43,300 --> 00:09:44,910
and you're not happy about it?

141
00:09:44,910 --> 00:09:46,690
What friend?

142
00:09:46,860 --> 00:09:48,120
He's just a criminal.

143
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:53,580
Actually,

144
00:09:53,980 --> 00:09:56,710
I called him here because
I have something to say.

145
00:09:57,960 --> 00:09:59,290
What is it?

146
00:10:00,080 --> 00:10:01,250
Ah.

147
00:10:01,450 --> 00:10:02,280
Oh.

148
00:10:02,460 --> 00:10:03,190
Are you okay?

149
00:10:03,230 --> 00:10:06,430
Memory, memory, memory.

150
00:10:10,420 --> 00:10:11,810
In the past...

151
00:10:13,050 --> 00:10:14,480
You two.

152
00:10:16,290 --> 00:10:17,780
You fought.

153
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:19,220
You two fought.

154
00:10:20,340 --> 00:10:22,090
You used to fight over me
all the time in high school.

155
00:10:22,090 --> 00:10:23,560
Are you fighting again?

156
00:10:23,970 --> 00:10:25,560
You scared me.

157
00:10:25,820 --> 00:10:27,080
Stop fighting.

158
00:10:27,200 --> 00:10:28,380
We're all friends.

159
00:10:29,060 --> 00:10:30,500
I'm sorry.

160
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:33,980
I'm sorry, Adolph.

161
00:10:49,210 --> 00:10:51,520
I let you get hurt.

162
00:10:51,770 --> 00:10:53,530
And I took your song.

163
00:10:56,670 --> 00:10:58,970
I coveted everything you had.

164
00:10:59,910 --> 00:11:01,120
I'm sorry.

165
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:04,210
I'm really sorry, Adolph.

166
00:11:07,550 --> 00:11:08,720
Yeah.

167
00:11:09,720 --> 00:11:11,230
You should be sorry.

168
00:11:12,430 --> 00:11:13,730
But...

169
00:11:19,020 --> 00:11:20,200
Adolph.

170
00:11:28,770 --> 00:11:30,300
Are you just going to say it?

171
00:11:35,020 --> 00:11:36,220
Take it out.

172
00:11:37,900 --> 00:11:39,910
I'm telling you to take out your wallet.

173
00:11:39,910 --> 00:11:41,590
Is a verbal apology enough?

174
00:11:41,990 --> 00:11:43,320
You're a complete thug.

175
00:11:43,390 --> 00:11:44,860
Hurry up and take it out.

176
00:12:00,310 --> 00:12:01,550
You two,

177
00:12:01,860 --> 00:12:03,910
make up already.

178
00:12:05,280 --> 00:12:06,410
I'm leaving.

179
00:12:07,090 --> 00:12:08,520
Hurry up.

180
00:12:43,500 --> 00:12:44,440
Oh.

181
00:12:45,940 --> 00:12:47,010
Where's Hanyul?

182
00:12:47,750 --> 00:12:49,840
With Herod, in the ward.

183
00:12:52,710 --> 00:12:53,660
Um,

184
00:12:55,310 --> 00:12:57,490
buy me some ice cream.

185
00:13:00,750 --> 00:13:03,480
What the hell? It's not even
expensive ice cream.

186
00:13:07,450 --> 00:13:09,250
Is it okay to leave them alone?

187
00:13:11,490 --> 00:13:13,580
I don't mind.

188
00:13:13,830 --> 00:13:16,240
You're the one who should mind.

189
00:13:18,780 --> 00:13:20,130
Can you...

190
00:13:22,310 --> 00:13:24,040
forgive Herod?

191
00:13:25,820 --> 00:13:27,080
Forgive?

192
00:13:28,210 --> 00:13:30,470
I can't say for sure.

193
00:13:31,050 --> 00:13:33,870
But I owe him too.

194
00:13:36,770 --> 00:13:39,050
This kid probably has some good stuff
in his bag.

195
00:13:39,050 --> 00:13:41,500
Really? Let me see.

196
00:13:41,740 --> 00:13:43,560
Let go, damn it.

197
00:13:44,350 --> 00:13:45,730
Let go, you bastard.

198
00:13:45,870 --> 00:13:46,710
Let go!

199
00:13:46,960 --> 00:13:48,220
Hey, get out of the way.

200
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:50,560
Die, you bastard!

201
00:13:50,900 --> 00:13:52,830
It's too boring to end it like this.

202
00:13:53,420 --> 00:13:55,080
Would a guy's hole be tighter?

203
00:13:55,900 --> 00:13:58,400
He's a goody-two-shoes model student,
so I bet it is.

204
00:13:58,400 --> 00:14:00,200
Hey, everyone get out of the way.

205
00:14:04,630 --> 00:14:05,810
I'm sorry.

206
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:08,990
I know that no matter what I say,

207
00:14:09,120 --> 00:14:11,470
I can't make it up to you and Adolph.

208
00:14:19,140 --> 00:14:21,700
I will completely disappear
from your sight.

209
00:14:24,930 --> 00:14:26,250
You know what?

210
00:14:34,350 --> 00:14:36,630
I was there too.

211
00:14:39,680 --> 00:14:42,430
[See you at the gym at 10 tonight!]

212
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:42,650
See you at the gym at 10 tonight.

213
00:14:47,390 --> 00:14:48,780
Hey, is he really dead?

214
00:14:48,910 --> 00:14:49,950
Whatever.

215
00:14:50,110 --> 00:14:51,480
He's just an orphan anyway.

216
00:14:51,480 --> 00:14:53,180
No one will know if he's gone.

217
00:14:53,310 --> 00:14:54,580
Oh, you're here.

218
00:14:54,700 --> 00:14:55,690
Funny, right?

219
00:14:56,910 --> 00:14:58,980
Look at his face. It's hilarious, right?

220
00:14:58,980 --> 00:15:01,530
Composing music, yeah right. When I saw him
playing the piano in the piano room

221
00:15:01,530 --> 00:15:02,990
I already thought he was super annoying.

222
00:15:02,990 --> 00:15:04,920
It's too boring to end it like this.

223
00:15:05,500 --> 00:15:07,160
Would a guy's hole be tighter?

224
00:15:07,280 --> 00:15:10,210
He's a goody-two-shoes model student,
so I bet it is.

225
00:15:25,180 --> 00:15:27,150
I didn't save him.

226
00:15:28,190 --> 00:15:29,950
I chose to run away.

227
00:15:32,990 --> 00:15:34,500
Actually, you and I

228
00:15:34,950 --> 00:15:36,680
are essentially the same.

229
00:15:37,830 --> 00:15:40,290
So you don't have to
apologize to me anymore.

230
00:15:43,850 --> 00:15:47,860
I was beaten by those classmates
until I lost my memory.

231
00:15:48,030 --> 00:15:51,060
When I finally woke up again later,

232
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:55,210
the first thing I saw

233
00:15:56,060 --> 00:15:58,020
was Herod's bare feet running

234
00:15:58,380 --> 00:16:00,430
with me on his back.

235
00:16:02,240 --> 00:16:03,570
Adolph!

236
00:16:03,970 --> 00:16:05,020
Are you okay?

237
00:16:05,430 --> 00:16:06,790
Hold on a little longer.

238
00:16:09,110 --> 00:16:12,040
And then I lost my memory again.

239
00:16:13,240 --> 00:16:17,050
When I woke up from time to time,

240
00:16:18,010 --> 00:16:23,020
Herod was always by my hospital bed.

241
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:26,870
Herod really likes Hanyul.

242
00:16:27,530 --> 00:16:29,190
He must be very anxious.

243
00:16:29,550 --> 00:16:34,490
He probably did imagine
how nice it would be without me.

244
00:16:34,940 --> 00:16:39,560
But even if he had such thoughts,
he must've been in a lot of pain himself.

245
00:16:40,440 --> 00:16:42,560
Liking someone

246
00:16:42,970 --> 00:16:45,090
makes you really happy,

247
00:16:45,450 --> 00:16:47,580
but it's also something unfortunate.

248
00:16:52,860 --> 00:16:55,940
I wonder if they've made up by now.

249
00:17:05,579 --> 00:17:06,630
Here.

250
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:22,240
Thank you.

251
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:25,040
But why aren't you
giving it to him yourself?

252
00:17:25,040 --> 00:17:26,900
Aren't you here to give him this?

253
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:29,860
I promised Hanyul

254
00:17:30,770 --> 00:17:32,770
that I would help get your song back.

255
00:17:34,640 --> 00:17:36,350
Are you going somewhere?

256
00:17:51,180 --> 00:17:52,360
Where's Herod?

257
00:17:52,610 --> 00:17:53,680
Huh?

258
00:17:54,380 --> 00:17:55,630
He left.

259
00:17:55,870 --> 00:17:58,500
Terrible, leaving you all alone.

260
00:18:02,980 --> 00:18:03,970
Ta-da.

261
00:18:04,290 --> 00:18:05,170
What's this?

262
00:18:05,270 --> 00:18:06,680
Isn't this your sheet music?

263
00:18:05,540 --> 00:18:06,680
["Sound of Dawn" by Adolph]

264
00:18:07,040 --> 00:18:10,100
The great composer Lee
gave it to me at the door just now.

265
00:18:10,330 --> 00:18:12,090
He said he promised you

266
00:18:12,270 --> 00:18:14,280
that he would help get this song back.

267
00:18:14,280 --> 00:18:15,940
Was he here?

268
00:18:16,710 --> 00:18:18,970
Then why didn't he give it to me directly?

269
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:20,240
Tell me about it.

270
00:18:20,360 --> 00:18:21,670
How would I know?

271
00:18:27,900 --> 00:18:32,570
[Hanyul]

272
00:18:50,220 --> 00:18:51,480
Lee Won!

273
00:18:51,920 --> 00:18:54,130
